{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/871041-werewolves-mamuts","id":871041,"title":"Werewolves & Mamuts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-22T01:13:00-07:00","id":871041,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon6.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Werewolves & Mamuts","content":"I saw this Exalted graphic...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/PJL7YMu.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> How can I make it true in <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b>? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T05:10:07-07:00","id":871118,"title":"","content":"I would say the easiest form is to have a veru old spirit that went dormant via extinction of it's main fleshy reflection wake up after a scientific experiment that tried reviving a Mammoth by mixing it's DNA with that of an Elephant. The clone dies after a few days, but the Essence produced is enough to stir the giant into action. Then, the very powerful Spirit becomes a Magath by devouring too much at once to maintain itself active, rampaging through the Shadow in desperation and confusion.<br /> <br /> Do the Ithaeur put him down, even though it is a relic that can have new Gifts and Rites?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T05:21:33-07:00","id":871124,"title":"","content":"The guys with the antlers look like True Fae, or at least changelings or hobgoblins. If you decide to keep the wolf-people as werewolves, maybe some of them survived the Sundering by finding a new boss, for whom they work as hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T07:19:39-07:00","id":871183,"title":"","content":"Museum spirit.<br /> <br /> A Werewolf pack based in a museum - probably a lot of Iron Masters there, interested in the melting-pot experience you get when spirits from all over the world are jumbled together.<br /> <br /> Their Totem was born as the spirit of a model of a mammoth; it's a vast combination of Mammoth essence (because even a statue of a thing has some of the concept of the thing in it) and the various emotions it inspires - wonder, a touch of loss from people's feelings about extinct species, and small children's fear when they don't realise it isn't alive.<br /> <br /> It's <i>probably</i> not a Magath, it's just a museum piece, and museum pieces are quite complex.<br /> <br /> The pack are <i>probably</i> just interested in what happens in this sort of melting pot, where influences from all over can combine - they watch and value the things that manage to broaden out while keeping themselves stable, and they cull the ones that cross the line into warped madness.<br /> <br /> But that's all very difficult to explain when unfamiliar werewolves arrive.<br /> <br /> Iiiii kinda want to play that game now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T19:26:16-07:00","id":879181,"title":"","content":"Dark Eras will still not be old enough to have them. It's some 7 000 years between the vanishing of mammoths from Europe and the neolithic game period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T20:18:10-07:00","id":879209,"title":"","content":"Time travel? Maybe cloning?<br /> <br /> Alternatively... finding a &quot;Lost World&quot;, somewhere that time just forgot?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T21:07:22-07:00","id":879235,"title":"","content":"Considering we have time rips with dinosaurs appearing in the Amazon its completely possible to have mammoths doing the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T22:07:17-07:00","id":879277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/871041-werewolves-mamuts?p=879235#post879235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering we have time rips with dinosaurs appearing in the Amazon its completely possible to have mammoths doing the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, what?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Where it is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T22:18:07-07:00","id":879287,"title":"","content":"In Dark Eras in the Beneath the Skin section focused on Skinchangers and Demons set during the height of the Aztec Empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T05:30:38-07:00","id":879462,"title":"","content":"I don't know why... but I want mammoth shifters now. . Maybe based off thr Land Titans... though built with second ed rules and not the shitty changing breeds rules...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T12:04:15-07:00","id":879609,"title":"","content":"Actually it looks like from recent findings, there were still surviving mammoths in northern Siberia and Alaska much later than previously thought. So there would be some contemporary to Sundered World, First Turn Egypt, and Hunting Grounds Ancient Sumer -- just not anywhere near those locals.<br /> <br /> Seems reasonable to me to have Mammoth as an old fading Pangean in Sundered World, foreshadowing what Wolf will become if the Uratha don't do something...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-01-2016, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T14:15:23-07:00","id":881255,"title":"","content":"There are still dinosaur spirits around according to the Rockies book, so Mammoth spirits still being around would hardly be an impossibility.<br /> <br /> The antler guys do seem most like fae, but there were the deer skinning &quot;lords of the hunt&quot;from Skinchangers, perhaps expanding them into a shapeshifter type from War Against the Pure, perhaps the chosen of Cernunnos or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}